<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Turkmenchay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1828">1828</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-persian-war-1826-1828">Russo-Persian War (1826–1828)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Turkmenchay, signed in February 1828, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-persian-war-1826-1828">Russo-Persian War</a> of 1826 to 1828. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> ceded the khanates of Erivan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhichevan</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, confirmed earlier losses such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talysh">Talysh</a>, paid a large indemnity and granted Russian subjects legal privileges. It fixed the Aras river as the frontier and encouraged Armenian migration into the ceded lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-turkmenchay.jpg" alt="Treaty of Turkmenchay" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vladimir Moshkov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Treaty_of_Turkmenchay_by_Moshkov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
